> 2. What are statues, sinks, altars and wells/fountains (good) for?

Statues: sometimes these are traps: monsters posing as a statue. Normally,
they just act as dungeon decoration, but sometimes, there's something
hidden *inside* (not under) them.

Fountains: one can not only dip, but also quaff from them. Most hardy
perennials in this group will advise against this, by the way, the
possible positive effects by far do not outweigh the negarive outcomes.

Altars: there are so many uses for these, that I won't go into them here.
See the above site for more information and tips.

Sinks: mostly useless. Floating over them will sometimes help, and you can
kick them (be prepared for negative results). Dropping an unidentified
ring in them will give a message that will hint to the type of ring.

